  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Deliver M3-W01-C02-T1 as a new standalone .NET 10 numerics package with immutable finite binary64 dense matrices and vectors, bounded scalar work, canonical sparse coordinate strategy, explicit approximate IR transport and copied provider-array interchange. Verify independent absent-contract RED, seventeen arithmetic/boundary GREEN tests, a real managed Math.NET 5.0.0 copy-bridge solve/residual, locked solution and existing Math regressions, plus local NuGet package dependency/assembly graph.",
    "value": "Math gains real provider-neutral approximate matrix/vector addition, multiplication and sparse storage with hand-checkable numerical oracles, shape/budget rejection and explicit IR/providercopy boundaries, without making third-party Math.NET types or packages public Math dependencies.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "M3-W01-C02-T2 stays planned: qualify explicit rational-to-double conversion, advanced alias safety, sparse/provider strategy and optional-provider loading before C02 completion.",
      "Only finite approximate binary64 is admitted. Exact rational IR is rejected rather than silently widened; no algebraic exactness or cross-platform floating bitwise equivalence is implied.",
      "Managed Math.NET 5.0.0 appears only in a test-only adapter smoke, not in the new public dw.tools.math.numerics NuGet dependency graph.",
      "Matrix storage is limited to 4096 cells; multiplication has a separate 65536-scalar-product quota. Nonfinite intermediate arithmetic is rejected.",
      "No native BLAS, unexecuted RID, symbolic solver, AURA permission or external consumer adoption is claimed."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After RS040 success, qualify M3-W01-C02-T2 boundaries: reported rational-to-binary64 precision loss, strict copy-versus-alias guarantees and no provider load-time dependency; close C02 only after independent RED/GREEN.",
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T1-R",
        "achievement": "An independent compiled test observes the missing provider-neutral numerical matrix public contract before installing any numerical implementation."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T1-G",
        "achievement": "Immutable, provider-free finite binary64 dense/sparse matrices and vectors implement shape-checked addition, multiplication, dot product, canonical sparse coordinates and approximate-only typed IR conversion with explicit budgets."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T1-V",
        "achievement": "Seventeen independent numerical GREEN tests, managed Math.NET 5.0.0 copy-bridge solve/residual, prior regressions, locked build and verified local package demonstrate the qualified T1 scope."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T1",
        "achievement": "The numerical matrix/vector contract and outcome task is qualified while provider loading, explicit exact-to-approximate policy and stronger aliasing remain for T2; neither C02 nor M3 is closed."
      }
    ]
  },
